    {
      "id": "interaction-smoke-procedure",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Phase 2 Procedure",
      "root": false,
      "position": {"x": -860, "y": -180},
      "width": 520,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {"id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270},
        {"id": "right", "label": "right", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 0},
        {"id": "bottom", "label": "bottom", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 90}
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Phase 2 Procedure",
        "markdown": "# Phase 2 Procedure\n\nUse this graph on `dev.twilite.zone` in edit mode.\n\n1. Drag empty canvas: the canvas pans.\n2. Drag the unpinned card: only that node moves.\n3. Drag the pinned card background: the canvas pans.\n4. Scroll inside the long card: its content scrolls until the boundary, then wheel zoom becomes reachable.\n5. Drag connection and resize handles: each handle keeps ownership.\n6. Hover and click the labeled edges: the intended edge highlights and selects.\n7. Open the People portal and confirm its pager controls remain clickable.\n8. Save, reload, and confirm the authored pin survives.\n\nDo not accept a renderer-local propagation patch as a passing result.",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {"graphId": "interaction-arbiter-smoke"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "interaction-smoke-unpinned",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Unpinned Node",
      "root": false,
      "position": {"x": -180, "y": -120},
      "width": 430,
      "height": 270,
      "ports": [
        {"id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270},
        {"id": "right", "label": "right", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 0},
        {"id": "bottom", "label": "bottom", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 90},
        {"id": "left", "label": "left", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 180}
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Unpinned Node",
        "markdown": "# Unpinned Node\n\nDragging this background moves the node. Handles, text, and chrome must retain their own behavior.",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {"graphId": "interaction-arbiter-smoke"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "interaction-smoke-pinned-scroll",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Pinned Scroll Surface",
      "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 420, "y": -120},
      "width": 470,
      "height": 330,
      "positionLocked": true,
      "ports": [
        {"id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270},
        {"id": "right", "label": "right", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 0},
        {"id": "bottom", "label": "bottom", "direction": "output", "dataType": "value", "angle": 90},
        {"id": "left", "label": "left", "direction": "input", "dataType": "value", "angle": 180}
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Pinned Scroll Surface",
        "markdown": "# Pinned Scroll Surface\n\nDragging unused card background pans the canvas; it never selects text or moves this node.\n\n## Internal scrolling\n\nWheel input over this content belongs here while more content remains in that direction. At the scroll boundary, the canvas must regain wheel zoom.\n\n## Controls and chrome\n\nPin, Edit, links, inputs, and resize or connection handles remain interactive even though the node is pinned. Pinning transfers only background movement ownership.\n\n## Reload proof\n\nSave and reload. This card must remain pinned because `positionLocked` is authored graph state.\n\n## Regression warning\n\nA fix that works only for one renderer, one zoom level, or one mouse path does not pass.",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "identity": {"graphId": "interaction-arbiter-smoke"}
      }
    },
